[statement]
apk tells packages apart by their identity alone: a record with the
identity of a record of another name, read before it, is no package of
its own. `two` has the identity of `one`, so apk has no package for the
name `two`, and refuses.

[repository]
C:Q1AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA=
P:one
V:1

C:Q1AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA=
P:two
V:1

[request]
two

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   two (no such package):
|     required by: world[two]
refused
